// Build-A-Player College Football tight ends: generated by the CFB TE data build (F:/bap-agents/college/te: fetch.py,
// teamstats.py, grade.py, ovr-entry.js, headshots.mjs, write.py), ESPN feeds pulled 2026-11-13.
// Do not hand-edit counts; re-run the build. Read with data/cfb-players.js (the same row shape and the same scale).
//
// ── Who is here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every 2026 FBS team (138): TE1 and TE2 from ESPN's rosters (position TE) and 2026 game logs (every game through
// Week 11). 270 rows: 138 TE1s, 132 TE2s (a team whose second tight end has never caught a college pass has none).
// TE1 is the one with the most 2026 production (catches plus yards / 10, the last three games counted twice); a team
// whose tight ends have no 2026 catches would take its most experienced one (none needed it this year).
// Bio (number, height, weight, class) and photo: ESPN. espn = the ESPN athlete id. year: ESPN's roster class (no RS-
// flag: the redshirt audit the QB/WR/RB rows had was not run here).
// s26 / s25: his 2026 (to date) and 2025 lines from ESPN (gp = games with a recorded stat in his 2026 game log).
// skin: the median skin-coloured pixel of his ESPN headshot's face box (the figure's skin when his chip is on a build).
//
// ── Grade scale (the NFL 0-11 scale, read against college players, as data/cfb-players.js) ────────────────────
//   0 F · 1 D · 2 C- · 3 C · 4 C+ · 5 B- · 6 B · 7 B+ · 8 A- · 9 A · 10 A+ · 11 S
//   Checked on the output (average trait grade, size included): P4 TE1 6.9 · G6 TE1 5.7 · TE2 5.0 (the QB/WR/RB files:
//   P4 starters 6.3-6.8, G6 5.5-5.9, backups 5.0-5.4). College OVR (utils/cfbOvr.js), TE1 p10 / median / p90 / max:
//   75 / 81 / 89 / 99, against the WR1-3 rows' 77 / 82 / 89 / 99; eight rows at 95+ (the WRs: eight).
//
// ── How a grade is made (grade.py) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. Stats: 2026 to date (weight 1.0 a catch), 2025 (0.6) and 2024 (0.35) from ESPN's athlete stats; the team's 2026
//    completions, passing yards and games from ESPN's team statistics.
// 2. Per-catch rates (yards and touchdowns a catch, the longest catch) are regressed toward the pool's by catches
//    (30 catches of the pool rate; 15 for the longest catch), then each stat is a z-score among the TEs with 12+
//    weighted catches.
// 3. Each trait's evidence is a weighted mix (below), re-standardized so every trait has the same spread.
// 4. HIS LEVEL (the College Basketball file's step 3): what he produces. 0.4 share of his team's 2026 receiving yards,
//    0.35 catches a team game, 0.25 touchdowns a catch, shrunk toward a role prior by weighted catches
//    (n / (n + 18); prior z TE1 -0.2, TE2 -0.8), + 0.25 for a Power 4 schedule (Notre Dame included), -0.2 otherwise.
//    A trait is 0.62 x his level + 0.5 x (that trait's evidence minus the average of his traits' evidence): the level
//    decides how good he is, the evidence what he is good at. (Graded on traits alone, a 265-lb backup with 19 catches
//    was the country's best tight end on his frame.)
// 5. grade = 5.7 + 1.05 x 1.95 x z (x 0.85 below average) + 0.4 x max(0, z - 1)^2, rounded, 0-11; 11 (S) needs
//    z >= 3.1 (the WR curve, with the top eased: per-catch evidence runs hotter at tight end).
// 6. Size is physical, from ESPN height/weight on the NFL file's own TE scale (data/tes.js, te-legends.js): 70% height,
//    30% weight, 74 in / 235 lb = 0, 79 in / 264 lb = 11.
// ovr: the game's own formula (utils/simulation.js calcOVRTE); the mode shows it through the college curve.
//
// Trait evidence (z-scores; "-" = lower is better). ESPN has no college targets, drops, routes or blocking grades, so
// Blocking and Strength are read from the frame and experience (they move with his level like every trait):
//   speed: yds/catch .45, longest catch .3, -weight .25      vertical: TD/catch .35, yds/catch .3, height .35
//   routeRunning: share of team completions .45, catches/game .3, yds/game .25
//   hands: share of team completions .5, catches/game .3, career catches .2
//   awareness: career catches .4, TD/catch .3, catches/game .3      afterCatch: yds/catch .5, longest catch .3, weight .2
//   blocking: weight .55, height .2, career catches .25      strength: weight .7, height .3
//
// ── Headshots (ESPN only) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 266 rows have one: ESPN's college-football photo (headshots.mjs, the scripts/fetch-cfb-assets.mjs way: ESPN's combiner,
// 350x254 crop, webp q75, public/headshots/cfb_{id}.webp). The rest show initials. Contact sheets were looked at.

